# Build context for antithesis/Dockerfile is this directory (the repo root),
# because the pxc-node image builds PXC from source.
#
# Keep exclusions minimal — anything removed here that the build needs fails
# deep inside a long cmake run. Only genuinely build-irrelevant things go below.

# Version control metadata. No build step needs it: the galera version is
# parsed from GALERA_VERSION, and the one place cmake shells out to git
# (storage/rocksdb, for version stamping) is guarded by an EXISTS check on a
# .git that is not present anyway.
#
# `**/.git` matters as well as `.git`: submodule .git entries are *files*
# holding "gitdir: ../.git/modules/...", which would point at the excluded
# top-level .git and dangle inside the image. Excluding them keeps any stray
# git invocation failing cleanly with "not a repository" instead of chasing a
# broken pointer.
.git
.git/**
**/.git
.hg
.hg/**

# Local build output, if anyone has built in-tree.
/build
/bld
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode — would otherwise be copied into the workload image and into
# /opt/antithesis/catalog/, which Antithesis scans for assertions.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Build logs. These live in the repo root and change on EVERY build, so without
# this they alter the `COPY . /src` layer checksum and invalidate the entire
# compile cache — galera and the full cmake build would re-run every time even
# when no source changed.
*.log
**/*.log

# This file itself. It sits at the context root, OUTSIDE antithesis/, so the
# pxc-src stage would otherwise carry it into /src and every edit here would
# invalidate the entire compile — the exact problem pxc-src exists to prevent.
.dockerignore

# Same reasoning as .dockerignore above, and the same trap: .gitignore sits at
# the context root, OUTSIDE antithesis/, so pxc-src does NOT strip it and it
# lands in /src. Editing it therefore changes the tree handed to pxc-build and
# invalidates the entire galera + server compile. That is not hypothetical --
# this workflow edits it (the `local-validate**.log` entry was added for
# exactly the log files *.log above excludes). No build step reads it.
.gitignore
